# Line endings: git detects text files, stores them with LF and checks them out with the
# platform's native endings. Unity reads either. Without this, CRLF and mixed files built up.
* text=auto

# Binaries shipped in the repo (git would detect most of these; being explicit is cheaper
# than a corrupted plugin).
*.png    binary
*.PNG    binary
*.Png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.wav    binary
*.mp4    binary
*.dll    binary
*.so     binary
*.dylib  binary
**/*.bundle/** binary

# Unity YAML (scenes, prefabs, assets) is merged with Unity's Smart Merge as a git mergetool,
# not as a merge driver: a driver gets extension-less temp files, which UnityYAMLMerge does not
# recognise. See README, "Merging scenes and prefabs".

# The one Unity asset Unity still writes in binary despite Force Text.
ProjectSettings/NetworkManager.asset binary
